    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-nĕco</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to kill</i>, <i>destroy</i> (ante- and post-class.; cf.: interficio, trucido,
			etc.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">internecatis hostibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 1, 34, 6</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sementes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 6, 50</span></i>
			: culmum, Prud. prooem. Apoth. 61.</div>
